{
  "comment": "Column order of the three tables a unique item's NAME is joined out of, from poe-tool-dev/dat-schema (PoE2 entries; its CI republishes schema.min.json on every commit). Offsets are NOT stored - they are arithmetic over the widths in DatColumns, and recomputing them is what keeps this honest when a width is corrected; the interval rule that cost Mods a whole table is one such correction. THE JOIN: UniqueStashLayout carries a WordsKey and an ItemVisualIdentityKey, Words holds the unique's name as Text, and ItemVisualIdentity's Id is the key the game exposes on the item itself at Base+0x30 - which is why the name is reached this way round rather than from the metadata path, and why a German client still prices its uniques in English. IsAlternateArt breaks the tie where two layout rows name one art. WHAT IS NOT VERIFIED HERE, said plainly: none of these three is in the loader's file table, so unlike BaseItemTypes and Mods their row size cannot be checked against a running client. The check is the FILE's own row size, which a .dat declares by where it puts its separator, and it happens at runtime against a real install - LoadedTable.Agrees, and the readout says which way it went. The sizes these columns compute are UniqueStashLayout 83 (0x53), Words 64 (0x40), ItemVisualIdentity 968 (0x3C8).",
